// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Author: Simone Machetti
//
// Description:
//   Power-stimulus testbench for the square N x N PE grid, top_NxN_sqr. It drives
//   activity, it does not check results - the functional proof is tb_top_NxN_sqr.
//   Purpose is to produce an activity.vcd for post-synthesis power analysis
//   (make post-syn-sim VCD=1, then make post-syn-dpa).
//
//   Stimulus: NUM_STREAM random operand sets per mode, streamed one per clock
//   with every row and column enabled, single-shot only - sel_acc is tied low,
//   acc is zero, and no rectangle scaling is exercised. The grid is reset once
//   at the start, then the modes run back to back with no reset and no idle
//   between them. Dumping starts after reset deassertion, so the VCD holds only
//   the busy window and the reset transient is not charged to the average. A
//   final drain of LAT clocks lets the last operands reach out_q.
//
//   Mode tables and operand packing are those of tb_top_NxN_sqr. The operand values
//   are NOT: rand_signed here is uniform over the full signed range, while the
//   functional bench biases 40% of draws onto the two extremes to reach
//   sign-consistency corners - which for power only manufactures toggles.
//   Uniform independent operands with no reuse and no sparsity still make this
//   an upper bound on dynamic power, not a typical-workload figure.
//
// Parameters:
//   N          - grid side; the array is N x N PEs
//   NUM_STREAM - random operand sets streamed per mode; +vectors=<n> overrides
//   MODE_SEL   - -1 runs every mode into one VCD; a mode number (1,2,3,5..12)
//                runs that mode alone, for per-mode power; +mode=<m> overrides
//
// Defines:
//   CLK_PERIOD_NS - clock period in nanoseconds, supplied by the flow; the
//                   default of 10 (100 MHz) applies when it is not defined
//
// Plusargs:
//   +mode=<m>     - run one mode only, overriding MODE_SEL
//   +vectors=<n>  - operand sets per mode, overriding NUM_STREAM
//
//   Both are read at run time so a mode sweep reuses one compiled binary: the
//   build step dominates the cost of this bench by two orders of magnitude.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

`timescale 1 ns/1 ps

`ifndef CLK_PERIOD_NS
`define CLK_PERIOD_NS 10
`endif

